WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.169 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.337
-Happy Thanksgiving!

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.774
So, I sang the line,
"It's 5:00 on a Saturday,"

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:11.778
and was told the line
from Billy Joel's "Piano Man"

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:14.013
is, "It's 9:00 on a Saturday.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:17.150
That is true, but...

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.888
I was not singing "Piano Man,"
by Billy Joel.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:24.390
I was singing "Keyboard Guy,"
by Bobby Jake.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:29.195
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:32.432
[ Clears throat ]

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.999
All right.
So we had a monologue.

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:37.136
There was a story
in the news about a python

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:42.742
eating an alligator
that happened in, um...

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:45.445
where did it happen?
It happened...

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.546
Python eating an alligator.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.582
It happened
in one of the 50 states.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:52.052
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:58.157
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.157 --> 00:00:59.926
South-- it was
a Southern state, right?

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.495
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:08.101
Oh! It was Florida.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.736
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:13.139
[ Clears throat ]

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:16.609
The punch line was
a python eating an alligator,

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:19.412
or what's also known
as a Florida turducken.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:24.583
Now...people were upset
because a turducken

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:28.254
is three elements --
turkey, duck, chicken --

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:32.292
whereas a python
eating an alligator is only two.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.795
We forgot to mention that when
they cut the alligator open,

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.797
he had a little bit
of meth in him.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:44.504
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:48.808
So you can call it a Florida
turducken or a pyallimeth.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:52.278
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.546
Which is important to know,
because if you're ever in

00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:56.249
Florida, do not
refer to yourself

00:01:56.249 --> 00:02:00.353
as a polymath
because it sounds too close

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.822
to pyallimeth.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:06.759
You can get in trouble if you're
down in Florida and you're

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.894
being all braggy about yourself.

00:02:08.894 --> 00:02:10.796
"Oh, I consider myself
a bit of a Renaissance man.

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:13.733
You could say a polymath," and
someone's like, "Hey, Cletus."

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:16.569
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.372
"This feller fancies
he can eat a whole alligator."

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.141
And then...

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:26.178
In general, if you're
a polymath, don't say it.

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:30.416
Let other people say it.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:33.253
Ooh, Monday, we had a joke...

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:37.523
about a turkey with a knife.

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:39.124
And someone said --

00:02:39.124 --> 00:02:41.026
We were informed
the turkey would

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:46.832
hold a knife in its foot,
its claw, not its wing.

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:50.002
But it couldn't --
it couldn't hold the knife

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:51.370
in its claw 'cause that's where

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.239
it holds its gun!

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.775
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.211 --> 00:03:01.648
It's a tur-knife-gun.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:05.684
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.684 --> 00:03:07.120
This is fascinating to me.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.055
It's pronounced "gay-la"
if it's a noun, meaning a party.

00:03:10.055 --> 00:03:12.625
It's pronounced "ga-luh"
if it's an adjective

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.395
describing a party --
a gala affair.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.830
And if it's a party with
legal gambling and prostitution,

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.399
it's pronounced Nevada.

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:27.373
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.342
I was told I held

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:32.478
the Maryland state flag
upside down.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.713
This is how I held it last week.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:37.083
As you can see,
that is an eyesore.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:40.019
But this,
oh, yi yi, beauty, beauty.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.755
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.457
Also, this is
the only state flag

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.794
that's also
a Magic Eye poster.

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.829
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:52.865
If you stare at it long enough,
you see...

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.034
like, Maryland celebrities.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.837
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.572
Stringer Bell.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:04.877
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:09.315
Audience is still split
on tank-top week.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.817
Some people thought
that when I wore my tank top,

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:12.918
I looked scrawny.

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:14.754
One person said
my arms look so good,

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.055
it made them self-conscious.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.457
Again, we can decide.
Let's take a look.

00:04:18.457 --> 00:04:21.661
I don't --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:24.831
No, I think it's fi--
I think it's like average arms.

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.131
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.131 --> 00:04:31.337
I think it's average arms
for a late-night talk-show host.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.439
So, uh...

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:36.408
We joked -- we talked about
a guy wearing a stovepipe hat

00:04:36.408 --> 00:04:38.243
and how you could fit

00:04:38.243 --> 00:04:41.681
an entire week's worth
of pizza under the hat.

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:43.249
And someone said,
"That's not enough

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:46.686
pizza for a week."
It is if you intermittent fast.

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:47.820
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.688
If you don't know,
intermittent fasting

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:52.158
is a diet that also
doesn't work.

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.993
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.129 --> 00:05:00.799
We've been talking about
the supermarket chain Aldi.

00:05:00.799 --> 00:05:03.403
And, uh...

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:04.837
It just occurred to me today,
right?

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:08.974
I'm working on this --
my "Corrections" afternoon,

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:11.944
and...it occurred to me
how funny it would be

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:16.248
if Snoop Dogg had, like,
a partnership with Aldi,

00:05:16.248 --> 00:05:19.285
and, you know,
through Snoop Dogg,

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.921
they would offer all these
pretzels, all these chips

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:23.723
and Aldi's nuts.
[all deez nuts]

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:27.359
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.359 --> 00:05:30.028
Pretty proud of it.
Shoemaker and I share a wall.

00:05:30.028 --> 00:05:33.032
If you're wondering,
that's why, at 10:00 a.m.,

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.400
you heard me scream, "Eureka!"

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:38.470
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:42.008
But, guys, I do this sometimes.

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:45.177
I come up with a thing,
and I worry

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:48.380
I might not be the first guy
who came up with "Aldi's nuts."

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.450
And, sure enough, I, uh --
I took a look,

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.953
and, oof, the youth
of today have me beat.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.921
It was not --
Not by a long shot

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:58.591
did I get to
"Aldi's nuts" first.

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:02.294
So, uh, that is a joke
that left the station years ago.

00:06:02.294 --> 00:06:04.430
And because of that,
it's not like

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.833
I was gonna waste Tara's time

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:09.334
and have her make a graphic.

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:12.104
That would have looked
probably something like that.

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:18.010
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.845
♪ Mm-hmm ♪

00:06:19.845 --> 00:06:22.314
Oh, if Donald Trump
had fallen into a lake,

00:06:22.314 --> 00:06:24.517
we talked about you would not
be able to get him out

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.819
with a pool scoop.
You would need a winch.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:30.856
Shout-out to all the jackals
who wrote that if they couldn't

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:33.659
find a winch, that a panicked
Donald Trump would

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:37.196
probably insist
they go looking for one

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:40.600
and would scream, "Winch hunt."

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.636
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:45.504
There are no lawns in Japan.

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:48.540
I don't know what joke
I made that implied there were.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.609
But a lot of you told me
there aren't.

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:52.578
Apologies.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:56.582
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:59.051
The French Revolution happened
in the 18th century,

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:00.452
not to the 19th century.

00:07:00.452 --> 00:07:02.321
A lot of you were really mad
about us getting that wrong.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:03.956
But, guys, there were --

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.992
you could still
feel the repercussions

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:08.627
in the 19th century.
Okay?

00:07:08.627 --> 00:07:13.466
You don't have a revolution
and then just move on.

00:07:15.735 --> 00:07:17.303
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:19.271
'Cause it's awkward for a --

00:07:19.271 --> 00:07:21.874
You have to then live together.

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:22.975
You know?

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:25.244
You'll see people --
les poissons --

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:28.548
that you...
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.548 --> 00:07:30.116
You know, that you were on --
And you're like,

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:31.384
"Oh, you look familiar.

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:34.186
Did I perhaps see you
through a wall

00:07:34.186 --> 00:07:37.690
of stacked-up furniture?"

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.158
They stacked up a lot --
the most --

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:43.696
They said,
of all armed conflicts,

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:46.532
French Revolution had the most
walls of stacked-up furniture.

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:50.803
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:53.439
Hey, guys, we've been
talking about Frankenstein.

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:56.842
And based on some of
the plot details I discussed

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:58.711
last week, many of you jumped
to the conclusions

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:01.981
that I have never read the book
by Mary Shelley

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:04.216
and I've only seen

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:07.786
the 1931 horror movie.

00:08:07.786 --> 00:08:10.456
That is not true.
I did read the book.

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.892
But I went back, and I dug up
my copy of the book,

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:15.260
and I realized --
I realized what happened.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.762
I read this version.

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:20.266
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:28.508
Speaking of, someone wrote
about "Frankenstein,"

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:31.043
"The villagers
ostracized and persecuted

00:08:31.043 --> 00:08:34.780
a sensitive soul purely because
he was different,

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.182
and their behavior
cannot be excused.

00:08:37.182 --> 00:08:39.952
Sort of like
what Seth does with Wally."

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:44.657
[ Laughter ]

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:48.561
I would say Frankenstein does
remind me of Wally in that,

00:08:48.561 --> 00:08:52.297
once we started
putting Wally on camera,

00:08:52.297 --> 00:08:53.733
we created a monster.

00:08:53.733 --> 00:08:58.104
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.106 --> 00:09:03.275
Sometimes there's a comment
so succinctly written

00:09:03.275 --> 00:09:04.743
that I just want
to share it with you.

00:09:04.743 --> 00:09:07.479
Somebody wrote, "Seth clearly
knows nothing about the Moon."

00:09:07.479 --> 00:09:10.349
You got me.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.349 --> 00:09:12.451
I don't know a [bleep] thing
about the Moon.

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:13.619
And here's why.

00:09:13.619 --> 00:09:16.822
Everything you learn about it
ruins the magic.

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:18.590
[ Laughter ]

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:22.061
Talk to a Moon scientists
and they'll ruin everything.

00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:25.431
"There's no man in it.
It's not made of cheese."

00:09:25.431 --> 00:09:28.167
[ Laughter ]

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:31.170
"It's round."
Okay.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:34.407
Then how come I can draw it
on a piece of paper?

00:09:34.407 --> 00:09:37.442
[ Laughter ]

00:09:37.442 --> 00:09:39.678
Are there --
I just --

00:09:39.678 --> 00:09:42.048
I want to be the first --
I want to be --

00:09:42.048 --> 00:09:44.349
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.349 --> 00:09:46.318
You never hear of flat-mooners.

00:09:46.318 --> 00:09:48.287
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.287 --> 00:09:50.956
I'm gonna be a flat-mooner.

00:09:50.956 --> 00:09:53.292
Yeah, I did my own research.

00:09:53.292 --> 00:09:56.361
[ Laughter ]

00:09:56.361 --> 00:10:00.132
I mean, are flat-earthers,
flat-mooners, too?

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:03.335
It would be so weird
if they were, like, full on --

00:10:03.335 --> 00:10:05.904
they were good with
the Moon being round.

00:10:05.904 --> 00:10:08.574
I don't know.

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:10.075
"The Earth is flat."
"What about the moon?"

00:10:10.075 --> 00:10:11.677
"I'm not [bleep] crazy."

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:14.113
[ Laughter ]

00:10:14.113 --> 00:10:16.615
"Come on, dude."

00:10:16.615 --> 00:10:18.884
I did get waxing and waning
exactly backwards.

00:10:18.884 --> 00:10:24.089
Waxing means getting bigger,
waning means getting smaller.

00:10:24.089 --> 00:10:26.625
Wax on, wane off.
That was the right way.

00:10:26.625 --> 00:10:28.827
Do you want to do Miyagi?

00:10:28.827 --> 00:10:31.863
Might be --
[ Laughter ]

00:10:31.863 --> 00:10:33.832
Might be a fun way for everybody
to see on camera

00:10:33.832 --> 00:10:35.401
the first time.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:35.401 --> 00:10:38.404
Shoemaker...

00:10:38.404 --> 00:10:40.806
You're in the costume.
All right.

00:10:40.806 --> 00:10:43.909
[ Laughter ]

00:10:48.714 --> 00:10:51.082
Um...

00:10:51.082 --> 00:10:53.285
I wrote a joke about
Superman going into a bank

00:10:53.285 --> 00:10:57.189
and then coming out with his
underpants pulled over his head

00:10:57.189 --> 00:10:58.324
by the bank robbers.

00:10:58.324 --> 00:11:01.660
In my mind,
if you pulled

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:03.529
underpants over someone's head,
they would come down --

00:11:03.529 --> 00:11:04.930
You know, like,
you'd pull it down.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.333
This is what graphics
came up with.

00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:09.435
Just a [bleep] kickass hat.

00:11:09.435 --> 00:11:14.673
[ Laughter ]

00:11:14.673 --> 00:11:18.043
Just, like, a kryptonite-proof
bike helmet.

00:11:18.043 --> 00:11:19.745
[ Laughter ]

00:11:19.745 --> 00:11:21.347
So, again, shame on me.

00:11:21.347 --> 00:11:23.882
Roll down to graphics.
And I'm like,

00:11:23.882 --> 00:11:25.217
"Is that what you think

00:11:25.217 --> 00:11:27.086
Superman's underpants
look like?"

00:11:27.086 --> 00:11:28.086
And of course, they're all like,

00:11:28.086 --> 00:11:29.555
"What do you think
they look like?"

00:11:29.555 --> 00:11:33.425
[ Laughter ]

00:11:33.425 --> 00:11:35.027
Weirdos.

00:11:35.027 --> 00:11:38.563
[ Laughter ]

00:11:38.563 --> 00:11:40.799
All right.
I want to come clean about --

00:11:40.799 --> 00:11:43.002
Well, first of all, you know,
obviously, we're aware

00:11:43.002 --> 00:11:44.336
of the jackal mug.

00:11:44.336 --> 00:11:47.339
Very popular in the merch.

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:49.541
Someone sent me this.

00:11:49.541 --> 00:11:50.676
They just made this.

00:11:50.676 --> 00:11:54.947
Don't. Make. Better. Mugs.
Than. Us.

00:11:54.947 --> 00:11:57.583
[ Laughter ]

00:12:01.253 --> 00:12:03.021
But here's the thing.
You know, I said we were

00:12:03.021 --> 00:12:05.357
gonna do a sweepstakes
because I felt bad for

00:12:05.357 --> 00:12:07.292
our foreign viewers,
foreign jackals,

00:12:07.292 --> 00:12:10.162
who can't order, um...

00:12:12.464 --> 00:12:15.334
Can't order the mugs online
because NBC doesn't

00:12:15.334 --> 00:12:17.703
ship to other countries

00:12:17.703 --> 00:12:19.805
because, um...

00:12:19.805 --> 00:12:22.341
they just don't want
to monetize it.

00:12:22.341 --> 00:12:24.176
[ Laughter ]

00:12:24.176 --> 00:12:25.577
I say, "Don't you want
to monetize it?"

00:12:25.577 --> 00:12:27.513
And they say, "It's art."

00:12:27.513 --> 00:12:31.983
[ Laughter ]

00:12:31.983 --> 00:12:33.885
So, anyway, I said, "Hey.

00:12:33.885 --> 00:12:35.988
Everybody from overseas,
send in a postcard,

00:12:35.988 --> 00:12:37.923
and then I'll draw one out."

00:12:37.923 --> 00:12:39.959
Sweepstakes, right?

00:12:39.959 --> 00:12:44.296
And we'll send -- one lucky
foreign jackal

00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:47.099
is gonna get a mug.
And so anyway,

00:12:47.099 --> 00:12:49.601
I didn't check with anyone
when I did this.

00:12:49.601 --> 00:12:52.237
I don't run "Corrections"
by anybody.

00:12:52.237 --> 00:12:54.406
And for the last month
since I've done that,

00:12:54.406 --> 00:12:56.441
I've been having tons
of meetings with NBC's

00:12:56.441 --> 00:13:00.279
legal department, hours a day.

00:13:00.279 --> 00:13:04.250
And then, yesterday,
they said, "Here's the deal.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:08.587
Anyone who sent in a postcard
you have to send a mug to."

00:13:08.587 --> 00:13:10.522
And I said,
"How did this take a month?"

00:13:10.522 --> 00:13:13.659
And they said,
"We wanted to bill you a bunch."

00:13:13.659 --> 00:13:15.894
[ Laughter ]

00:13:15.894 --> 00:13:18.830
